  <name>Ultimate Pad Config</name>
  <summary>Configure the 8BitDo Ultimate 2 Wireless controller</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.miguelsanzbr">
    <name>Miguel Sanz</name>
  </developer>
  <description>
    <p>Ultimate Pad Config sets up the 8BitDo Ultimate 2 Wireless controller on Linux, without the vendor's software. It talks to the controller directly, through the 2.4G adapter or the USB cable, and saves every change on the controller itself.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Three custom profiles: create, rename, enable or disable</li>
      <li>Button remapping, including L4/R4 and the PL/PR back buttons</li>
      <li>Stick dead zones and range, trigger ranges, rumble strength and gyro mapping</li>
      <li>LED rings: theme, colours, speed and a colour per LED</li>
      <li>Live view of the pressed buttons, sticks and triggers, with the battery level</li>
      <li>Backup and restore of the whole configuration</li>
      <li>English and Brazilian Portuguese interface</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The device is reached through its hidraw node, which needs a udev rule installed once on the host system. The
      project page explains it and ships an installer script.</p>
    <p>This is an independent project, not affiliated with or endorsed by 8BitDo. The protocol was
      reverse-engineered for interoperability.</p>
  </description>
